    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d746-a2">

                <pb facs="0782" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg732"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1 in No.
                    248.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Madden to Fehmi Pasha.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                                1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to transmit under
                    cover of this dispatch a petition of Mr. Socrates A. Seferiades, a citizen of
                    the United States, and to request you to be so kind as to give as soon as
                    possible the requisite orders to whom it may concern in order that any claim or
                    complaint against the said Seferiades be referred to this consulate, in
                    compliance with the laws and with the treaties and capitulations in force.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. H. Madden.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
